course: dictionary
lesson: 4310
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, the words around the word, shows you which meaning the writer wants. Grommet is one of these words, so check the clues before you decide.
explain: «Glue ear is sticky fluid left behind the eardrum after a cold that muffles sound; it often clears by itself, and if not, tiny tubes called grommets may help.» The clues are glue ear, eardrum and sound, so a grommet here must be a tiny tube in the ear, not a ring in cloth.
explain: On a tent or a shoe, the clues are different: holes, cloth and laces. There, a grommet is a strong metal or plastic ring. Ask yourself which meaning fits the clues around the word.
explain: To check, put your meaning into the sentence. «Tiny tubes may help» makes sense in the ear sentence, but «tiny rings may help» does not.
fact: A grommet is a metal or plastic ring put in a hole in cloth, leather or paper to make the hole strong.
fact: In medicine, a grommet is a tiny tube a doctor puts in a child's eardrum to let fluid drain out and help hearing.
fact: «Glue ear» is sticky fluid behind the eardrum that can muffle sound; grommets are one way to help it.
fact: In Australia and New Zealand, a grommet (or grom) is slang for a young surfer or skateboarder.
fact: Context tells you which meaning of a word the writer wants.
exercise: Mum fixed a grommet into the hole in the tent cover so the rope would not tear the cloth. What is a grommet here? | A young surfer | A kind of fishing net | *A metal ring for a hole | A tiny tube in an eardrum
exercise: The doctor said Sam needed a grommet because of his glue ear. What is a grommet here? | A sticky sort of glue | A surfer learning the waves | A ring for tying laces | *A tiny tube in the ear to help hearing
exercise: A boy in Australia says, «Look at that grom riding the big waves!» What is a grom? | *A young surfer | A tiny tube for the ear | An old fisherman | A kind of cloud
test: The banner had metal grommets along the top so it could hang from the fence. What do the grommets do? | They are a kind of surfing move | They help people hear | They make the banner glow | *They make the holes strong
test: Ella had grommets fitted in her ears, and afterwards she could hear the clock tick again. Where were the grommets? | In her shoes | *In her ears | On her surfboard | On her curtains
exam: Which meaning fits? «The grommet paddled out early, hoping to catch the first wave.» | *A young surfer | A tiny tube in the ear | A cover for cables | A metal ring for a hole
